  "difficulty_level": "H3",
  "difficulty_reason": "Two independent readers A and B support H3 for the complete correlated boundary-event construction. With gamma-Poisson representation, coloring, Mecke and elementary beta identities allowed, the task still requires truncation of large atoms, a weighted dyadic reduction to localized second moments, same-color factorial-pair control, and removal/reinsertion of two Poisson atoms while retaining their contribution to both the color numerator and the total normalization. The gamma change of variables then controls the perturbed beta window uniformly at both simplex faces and across dyadic scales. Marginal beta estimates or an independent-radius assumption cannot substitute for this joint construction. The retained full local proof, rather than its status as an auxiliary lemma or the title of its application, determines H3.",
